#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:9
msgid "Reporting an issue — how-to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:12
msgid ""
"Issue reports help the ROS community identify bugs, suggest enhancements, "
"improve documentation, and resolve package-specific problems. This article "
"explains how to check whether an issue has already been reported and what "
"information to provide in a new issue. With this information, you can "
"provide clear, complete issue details in the right ROS repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:22
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:25
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:27
msgid ""
"**Code issue trackers**: in a repository under the `ROS organisation "
"<https://github.com/orgs/ros2/repositories>`__ or elsewhere on GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:28
msgid ""
"**Documentation issue tracker**: `ROS documentation repository <https://"
"github.com/ros2/ros2_documentation/issues>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:29
msgid ""
"**Catch-all issue tracker**: `top level ROS repository <https://github.com/"
"ros2/ros2/issues>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:32
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:34
msgid "There are no prerequisites."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:37
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:40
msgid "1 Identifying where to report the issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:42
msgid ""
"If you identify a bug, have a suggestion for enhancement, or a question "
"specific to one package, you can report an issue on GitHub. For example, if "
"you are following a :doc:`tutorial </First-Steps>` and come across an "
"instruction that doesn't work on your system, you can report an issue in the "
"`ROS documentation repository <https://github.com/ros2/ros2_documentation/"
"issues>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:45
msgid ""
"You can report code issues in the ROS repository for the package where the "
"error occurred. This is generally the last file listed in the stack trace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:48
msgid "You can search for ROS packages in the following locations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:50
msgid ""
"Core ROS 2 packages, found in the `ROS organisation <https://github.com/"
"ros2>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:51
msgid ""
"ROS binary packages, found on the `ROS Index <https://index.ros.org>`__, "
"which point to the appropriate GitHub repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:52
msgid "Source ROS packages which are located elsewhere on GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:54
msgid ""
"If it's not clear which issue tracker to use for a particular issue, report "
"the issue in the `top-level ROS repository <https://github.com/ros2/ros2/"
"issues>`__ and we'll have a look at it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:57
msgid "2 Checking the issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:59
msgid "Before opening an issue:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:61
msgid ""
"Check if other users have reported similar issues by searching across the "
"``ros2`` and ``ament`` GitHub organizations using, for example, this `search "
"query <https://github.com/search?"
"q=user%3Aros2+user%3Aament+turtlesim&type=Issues>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:62
msgid ""
"Check the `Robotics Stack Exchange <https://robotics.stackexchange.com/>`__ "
"to see if someone else has already reported your issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:64
msgid ""
"If your issue has not been reported, you can open an issue in the issue "
"tracker of the repository you have identified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:67
msgid "3 Reporting the issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:69
msgid ""
"When reporting an issue, use the following steps to make sure you include "
"enough information for another person to understand and (where relevant) "
"reproduce the issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:71
msgid "In the issue tracker of your selected repository, select **New issue**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:72
msgid ""
"From the options shown, select the issue type which is most appropriate for "
"the issue you are raising:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:74
msgid ""
"If you are in a ROS code repository or the top-level ROS repository, select "
"**Bug report** or **Feature request**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:75
msgid ""
"If you are in the ROS documentation repository, select **Documentation "
"issue**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:76
msgid ""
"Alternatively, if the specific ROS repository you are in has a unique issue "
"template, you can use that instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:78
msgid "Add a descriptive **Title** for the issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:80
msgid "**Bad**: \"rviz doesn't work\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:82
msgid ""
"**Good**: \"Rviz crashing looking for missing ``.so`` after latest apt "
"update\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:84
msgid ""
"Complete the remaining fields in the issue template, following the prompt "
"text shown and the formatting of any pre-filled fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:87
msgid "Additional information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:89
msgid ""
"If you are reporting a bug, consider providing a `short, self contained, "
"correct (compilable) example <https://sscce.org/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:90
msgid ""
"When discussing any compiling/linking/installation issues, provide the "
"version number of your compiler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:91
msgid "If relevant to your issue, you can also include your:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:93
msgid "ROS environment variables (``env | grep ROS``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:94
msgid "Backtraces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:95
msgid "Relevant config files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:96
msgid "Graphics card model and driver version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:97
msgid "``Ogre.log`` for rviz, if possible (run with ``rviz -l``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:98
msgid "Bag files and code samples which reproduce the problem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:99
msgid "GIFs or video clips to demonstrate the problem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:100
msgid ""
"Log files (see :doc:`/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging`) or "
"logs from the RQT console (see :doc:`/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/"
"Using-Rqt-Console/Using-Rqt-Console`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:102
msgid ""
"Also describe any troubleshooting which you have already attempted, for "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Reporting-an-issue.rst:104
msgid ""
"Upgrading to the latest version of the code, which may include bug fixes "
